    "result": "Perfect! The bug is now fixed. Here's what I did:\n\n## Summary\n\n**The Issue:** The `frai gate init --ci` command through the CLI wrapper wasn't passing the `--ci` flag to the underlying `frai-gate` executable, so the GitHub Actions workflow file wasn't being created.\n\n**Root Cause:** The `frai` CLI uses Commander.js and defines a top-level `--ci` option (line 605). When the `gate` subcommand was called, Commander parsed the `--ci` flag at the parent level before the gate subcommand could receive it, so the flag was lost in translation.\n\n**The Fix:** Modified the gate command handler in `/private/tmp/100-tricks-runs/d24/without/t1-flag-bug/r1/packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` (lines 737-755) to:\n- Use the original `process.argv` instead of relying on Commander's parsed arguments\n- Extract the arguments from the `gate` command onwards using `process.argv.slice(process.argv.indexOf('gate') + 1)`\n- Pass these raw arguments directly to the frai-gate CLI\n\n**Verification:** Rebuilt the package with `pnpm --filter frai build` and tested that running `frai gate init --ci` now correctly creates both:\n- \u2705 `FRAI-SPEC.md` \n- \u2705 `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml`",
